    MIT, stated in the repository README. Copyright: multica-ai, the owner of
    that repository, for the compilation. The underlying guidelines are Andrej
    Karpathy's public statements.

The repository ships no `LICENSE` file and GitHub reports no licence for it, so
this notice records the grant as the README makes it rather than reproducing a
file that does not exist. A licence stated plainly in a README is a grant by the
repository owner; it is weaker as evidence than a licence file, and that is why
the exact wording is written out here.

What we actually took, measured on 2026-08-18 by the eight-word shingle method
used for `loopx`: `core/PRINCIPLES.md` **P2** shares 55% of its windows with the
source and is a genuine copy of expression. **P3** shares none — the heading and
the idea are common, the text is ours, and our own `ATTRIBUTIONS.md` overstated
this until it was measured. Ideas are not the issue and never were; the wording
in P2 is, and MIT asks only that this notice travel with it, which it now does.

